{"articles":{"Badami":{"x":"Badami, formerly Vatapi, is a city in the Bagalkot district of Northern Karnataka, in Southern India. It is a historical place.","sights":[{"n":"Badami cave temples","k":"see","d":"The main attractions of Badami are its caves. There are four main caves. The first one, dedicated to Shiva, was excavated by the Chalukyas in 550 AD.","img":"6th - 7th century Badami cave temples layout exterior annotated.jpg","ll":[15.91833,75.685]},{"n":"Bhutanatha Temples (eastern group)","k":"see","d":"A cluster of sandstone shrines dedicated to the deity Bhutanatha, built between the 7th and 11th century CE.","img":"Bhutanatha temple in Badami, Karnataka, India.jpg","ll":[15.92083,75.68778]},{"n":"Bhutanatha Temples (northern/upper group)","k":"see","img":"Bhutanatha temple in Badami, Karnataka, India.jpg","ll":[15.92141,75.68707]},{"n":"Shivalaya Temples","k":"see","d":"When facing the museum, walk through the gate on your left and follow the path up the 300 stairs or so.","img":"Malegitti Temple Badami.jpg","ll":[15.9224,75.68402]},{"n":"Malegitti Shivalaya Temple","k":"see","d":"This temple is the oldest one of the town. It is built on a flat rock and offers a nice view on Badami.","img":"Malegitti Temple Badami.jpg","ll":[15.92369,75.68142]},{"n":"Banashankari Amma Temple","k":"see","d":"Temple in Cholachagudda, Bagalkot, Karnataka, India","img":"Shakambari temple near Badami.JPG","ll":[15.88722,75.705],"q":"Q4853950"},{"n":"Mahakuta group of temples","k":"see","d":"Temple complex in Bagalkot district, Belgaum division, Karnataka, India","img":"Mahakuta group of temples3 at Mahakuta.jpg","ll":[15.91667,75.75],"q":"Q283287"},{"n":"Agastya lake","k":"see","d":"Artificial lake in Karnataka","img":"Agastya Lake.jpg","ll":[15.92012,75.68638],"q":"Q134880784"}],"c":[15,32,1,17,35,2,21,38,13,24,39,30,24,38,52,22,32,81,21,30,100,21,30,101,21,30,107,19,30,77,17,30,23,15,30,3],"cs":"est"},"Bhagalpur":{"x":"Bhagalpur is a city and a district at the Ganges River, 